WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.791
As a video editor, I've worked on many types of projects,

00:00:02.791 --> 00:00:06.120
and the one thing they all have in common is the organization phase.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.732
Before we can start editing, we have to sift through and organize footage,

00:00:09.732 --> 00:00:12.219
review clips, and otherwise prepare our project files

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:13.580
according to our preferences.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.319
It's a vital, unskippable step, but it takes up time

00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:19.540
that I'd much rather spend doing the creative, fun part of the job.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.580
That's exactly the kind of task Premiere's AI Assistant is here to help with.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.480
Now when we open up a fresh project,

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.880
we can have the AI Assistant set it up for us exactly how we prefer.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.568
This way we can get started faster and stay on deadline,

00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:34.160
all while keeping us in control of the creative stuff.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.280
Let me show you how it works.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.040
The AI Assistant can be accessed in the Window menu.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.940
It will open in a new panel, giving us a place to enter our requests.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.660
It works just like any other panel and can be moved around or docked as we like.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.820
For this practice project, we'll ask the Assistant to organize our video footage for us.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.398
We have a lot of clips, and it would have taken us

00:00:55.398 --> 00:00:57.420
quite a while to go through and organize them.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:00.134
Instead, the Assistant will process the request,

00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:03.640
displaying all the steps it takes on its way to completing it.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.340
It works in the background, so we can continue working independently while we wait.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.171
Once it finishes, we can review the conversation

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.300
and choose how we want to proceed from there.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.940
In this case, we now have all of our clips organized by the day it was shot on.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:23.200
When we open a new chat, the Assistant offers a few suggestions for prompts it can complete.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.359
This one right here, where it will sort all of our clips

00:01:26.359 --> 00:01:29.800
into groups by dialogue takes and then list the corresponding line

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.311
in a marker above each group,

00:01:31.311 --> 00:01:33.240
is extremely useful for this project.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.020
So we're going to go ahead and click that to get it started.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.270
While that's processing, we can open a separate conversation with the Assistant

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.560
to keep each line of work organized and focused.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.740
Our previous chats can be revisited by opening the menu in the panel header.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.050
Each decision made by the Assistant includes its reasoning,

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.520
and expanding that will allow us to see why it did what it did.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.480
This way, we can easily catch and correct any misunderstandings.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.000
If we don't like what it chose to do, we can use the undo button.
